                            <comment id="16563159" author="golovashkin" created="Tue, 31 Jul 2018 05:42:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; I will fix the System.out.println issue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Outstanding, thank you!!&#160; I am assuming that would fix all 3 of them:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;  System.out.{ print(), println(), printf() }&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; And I am confused why would you use log4j in zeppelin&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Existent (large) code base.&#160;&#160;I should be able to rewrite it to use Java System.out exclusively (after you fix it), but if Zeppelin provided simpler ways to deploy existent Log4j Java-Spark based projects, that would be great.&#160; Log4j is&#160;&lt;b&gt;not&lt;/b&gt; a show stopper for us; but it would be nice (assuming it is possible to begin with) to let us configure our internal Log4j to redirect app master-node output to the console, and for Zeppelin to pick it up to show in the notebook output.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16563174" author="zjffdu" created="Tue, 31 Jul 2018 06:01:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes&#65292; fix all 3 of them.  But I would suggest you to use println of scala since interanlly it is scala repl not java repl, although System.out.println also works. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
